Line 5: "clientName" is text (made on line 2), but this is a number.
    set clientname to 5
                      ^
A name keeps the kind of value it was made with. To keep a number, make a new name for it.

Line 6: "HOURLY_RATE" is a constant, so it can't change.
    set hourly_rate to 1
        ^^^^^^^^^^^
It's kept on line 3. If it needs to change, make it with "let HOURLY_RATE be ..." instead of "keep".

Line 7: You already made "Late Fee" on line 4.
    let late fee be 3
        ^^^^^^^^
To change it, write "set Late Fee to ...".

Line 8: I don't know anything called "clientnam".
    say clientnam
        ^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "clientName"? You made it on line 2.

Line 11: "Add Tax" needs a number for "amount", but this is text.
    say add tax to "x"
                   ^^^
"amount" is a number because of line 10. An input has one kind of value everywhere; to make it clear, write it in the definition, like "to Add Tax to amount (a number):".

Line 12: "Add Tax" needs 1 value, but this gives it 0.
    say add tax
        ^^^^^^^
It's defined on line 9: "to Add Tax to amount".
